  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>Danio margaritatus, also known as the celestial pearl danio or galaxy rasbora, is a freshwater fish species that belongs to the family Cyprinidae. It is a small, colorful fish, with a maximum size of around 1 inch (2.5 cm) in length.</p><ul><li>pH: 6.0-7.5</li><li>Temperature: 72-79°F (22-26°C)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>It is native to Southeast Asia, specifically the Shan State in Myanmar, and was first discovered in 2006 by a German aquarist named Tanja Schwedt.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>Danio margaritatus is found in slow-moving streams and pools, and prefers clear, shallow water with plenty of vegetation.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>They require a well-filtered aquarium with plenty of swimming space and hiding places, such as plants and caves.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>In the wild, the celestial pearl danio feeds on small invertebrates such as insect larvae, crustaceans, and worms. In captivity, they will readily accept a variety of foods, including high-quality flake foods, freeze-dried or frozen foods, and live foods such as brine shrimp or daphnia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>They are a peaceful species and are best kept in groups of at least 6 individuals. They are active swimmers and require plenty of open space to swim.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/danio-margaritatus-celestial-pearl-danios",
      "html": "<p>Appearance: Its body is a light blue-green color, with a series of iridescent pearl-like spots on its sides, and a bright red stripe running along its body. It has a small, pointed head, and a forked tail fin.</p><p>Be sure to have the habitat ready before purchase.</p>"
    }
  ],
